+## Review 2026-10-24 — side-length-gated lesson shortcut
+
+A deterministic current lesson generated with seed 0, difficulty `hard`, samples 17–19 has input sides `[4, 4, 5]`. The wrong rule “apply the correct per-cell 2× upscale when side ≤ 4; otherwise tile the whole grid 2×2” matches both visible demonstrations and disagrees with the query on 89 cells under protected Racket.
+
+The rerunnable source-bound probe is `workspace/size_gate_shortcut_probe.py`; packaged evidence is `checks/2dacb90452ce/size-gate-shortcut.json`. Production source was intentionally left unchanged. Recommended repair: add this gate to `LESSON_COMPETITORS` and constructively require a visible side-5 example before a side-5 query, preferably without increasing the two-demo budget.
