+## Review 2026-10-24 — orientation-gated T shortcut
+
+A deterministic current lesson generated with seed 0, difficulty `medium`, samples 20–22 contains only `horizontal_bar_down` T objects in both visible demonstrations, then a `vertical_bar_right` T in the query. The wrong rule “recolor only T tetrominoes whose three-cell bar is horizontal” matches both demonstrations and disagrees with the protected-Racket query label on four cells.
+
+The rerunnable source-bound probe is `workspace/orientation_shortcut_probe.py`; packaged evidence is `checks/4537fc1035d2/orientation-shortcut.json`. Production source was intentionally left unchanged. Recommended repair: add the orientation-gated rule to lesson competitors and guarantee a side-facing T in the visible demonstrations before any side-facing query.
